
UNTMP(1)            UNIX Programmer's Manual             UNTMP(1)

NAME
     untmp - clean files out of /tmp

SYNOPSIS
     untmp [ user ]

DESCRIPTION
     _U_n_t_m_p removes all the files from /tmp owned by the invoker.
     It is useful for those developing programs which use tem-
     porary files or for stopping a C compilation cold.

     If a user name is given, then files in /tmp owned by that
     user are removed rather than the files owned by the invoker.

BUGS
     Only certain users may specify another user name here.

